  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Impacts of COVID-19 on Migration and Migrants from a Gender Perspective</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this research project is to explore and critically examine the short- and longer-term gender implications of COVID-19 impacts on migration and the well-being of migrants worldwide so as to inform policy and programmatic responses after the pandemic and in case of any future similar pandemic outbreak. In this view, the research project will analyse the impacts of COVID-19 on gender roles and dynamics through the different stages of the migration cycle, from departure from the country of origin, through migration journeys, up until the arrival and stay in the destination country and, if applicable, return to the country of origin. It will delve into different potential gendered implications from the COVID-19 impacts, with particular emphasis on socioeconomic ones. The project will start with a virtual inception workshop gathering leading academic and applied experts on the topic of gender and migration who will then each author different thematic chapters of the research report, the main output of this project. The research report will be launched at a conference in Ottawa where some authors will present their chapters and engage in discussion with the audience, as well as during virtual webinars organized across different time zones.</narrative>
  </description>
